[agent-assisted] The developer aimed to improve recall on the DialogNLI contradiction benchmark by adding a semantic comparison layer that could catch contradictions the graph-based detector missed. A Claude-powered tool was integrated that compares new notes against related prior notes to detect numeric, preference, and role contradictions, lifting recall from 54% to 70% while maintaining 100% precision. Fifteen misses remain where notes share no extracted entity overlap, and the next step deferred to future work is scaling evaluation to 500 samples.
